# overcast — sample environment file.
#
#   cp .env.example .env   # then fill in the keys/paths you have
#
# `.env` is gitignored (never commit real secrets). It is sourced by the LIVE
# real-data e2e suite (test/e2e/live/run.sh) and is a convenient place to keep
# provider creds for local CLI use. EVERYTHING here is OPTIONAL: each e2e case
# gates on what it needs and SKIPS (counted as pass) when a key/tool/clip is
# absent, so the suite runs green with any subset.

# ── Sense / brain providers ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default watch/listen backend (Cloudglue via the tinycloud CLI), also a pickable
# brain LLM. https://cloudglue.dev
CLOUDGLUE_API_KEY=
# Hugging Face — turnkey `see` captioner + `enhance`, model downloads for the
# local object detector, AND `enhance --ops separate` (local-models): pyannote
# diarization is a GATED model — accept its license at
# https://huggingface.co/pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1 then set this.
# https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
HF_TOKEN=
# fal.ai — `see` (florence-2 caption/OCR) + `enhance` toolbox: esrgan/deepfilternet3,
# `--ops separate` (fal-ai/sam-audio/separate), `--ops segment` (fal-ai/sam-3/image).
# https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys
FAL_KEY=
# ElevenLabs — `listen` (Scribe STT) + `enhance` (voice isolation). https://elevenlabs.io
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ── Website analytics (Vite / PostHog) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Public PostHog project key for the website. Vite only exposes VITE_* names.
# Copy these into site/.env or your hosting provider's site env settings.
VITE_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
VITE_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# ── OSINT sources (scan/capture/monitor) ───────────────────────────────────
# Web search: Tavily preferred, Brave as fallback (set either).
TAVILY_API_KEY=
BRAVE_API_KEY=
# Apify actors power: tiktok + x/twitter + instagram + telegram enumerate, lens
# reverse image search, and the opt-in facesearch source. tiktok/x/instagram
# fetch uses yt-dlp / direct CDN. https://apify.com
APIFY_TOKEN=
# Windy Webcams API — the `webcam` source (geolocated live public webcams). Free
# tier is enough for scan + still capture + monitor. https://api.windy.com/webcams
WINDY_API_KEY=
# Serper.dev — the `dork` source (Google dorking: real Google SERPs that HONOR
# operators like site:/filetype:/inurl:, unlike `web`). Authorized recon only.
# https://serper.dev
SERPER_API_KEY=
# Shodan — the `shodan` source (host/service/banner intelligence; search filters
# or a bare-IP host lookup). Authorized recon only. https://account.shodan.io
SHODAN_API_KEY=
# OPT-IN, SENSITIVE: set to 1/true/yes/on to also materialize the SCREENSHOTS Shodan
# captures from exposed RDP/VNC/HTTP/camera hosts (→ see/face/crop) and surface RTSP
# stream endpoints. These are real, unwitting exposed hosts — enabling is your
# acknowledgement of the privacy/ToS/legal weight. Off/unset = metadata + host page only.
# OVERCAST_SHODAN_SCREENSHOTS=
# gdelttv source needs no key (public GDELT TV API); dl uses yt-dlp on PATH.
# Forensic senses need no key — `exif` uses system `exiftool`, `verify` uses
# `c2patool` (both report needs_credentials / exit 13 when absent).
# Optional source overrides (defaults are fine — uncomment to change):
# OVERCAST_INSTAGRAM_ACTOR=
# OVERCAST_TELEGRAM_ACTOR=
# OVERCAST_LENS_ACTOR=
# OVERCAST_FACE_SEARCH_ACTOR=
# OVERCAST_X_ACTOR=
# OVERCAST_WEBCAM_API=              # Windy Webcams API base URL override
# APIFY_RUN_SYNC_TIMEOUT_MS=        # run-sync budget for the Apify-backed sources

# ── Test media (LIVE e2e) — one full path per file ─────────────────────────
# Point each at a real local file (absolute path). No file names are baked into
# the repo. A case SKIPS when its file is unset or missing, so fill in only what
# you have.
# Videos:
OC_VIDEO_VISUAL=/path/to/screen-recording.mp4     # rich on-screen visual (~30s) — watch / see
OC_VIDEO_OBJECTS=/path/to/people-and-objects.mp4  # people + detectable objects — see --detect
OC_VIDEO_SMALL=/path/to/small-clip.mp4            # short / small — enhance / view
OC_VIDEO_SPEECH=/path/to/clip-with-speech.mp4     # clear spoken audio — listen (audio fallback)
# Standalone image + audio (used directly by see / listen; if unset, those fall
# back to a frame / audio extracted from the videos above):
OC_IMAGE=/path/to/photo.jpg                       # image — see (caption / OCR / detect)
OC_AUDIO=/path/to/recording.m4a                   # audio — listen

# Forensics real-data e2e (test/e2e/live/cases/34_forensics.sh): exif metadata/GPS
# + verify C2PA + map + geocode + devices. A GEOTAGGED photo unlocks the GPS →
# map/geocode legs; without it those self-skip (exif/verify/devices still run on
# OC_IMAGE / a video frame). exif needs system exiftool; verify needs c2patool.
OC_EXIF_IMAGE=/path/to/geotagged-photo.jpg        # real photo w/ embedded GPS + device tags
# OC_EXIF_IMAGE_2=/path/to/photo-same-camera.jpg  # optional: 2nd photo, SAME camera (device-linking serial cluster)

# Local visual DB real-data e2e (test/e2e/live/cases/16_visual_db.sh):
OC_LOCAL_FACE_VIDEO=/path/to/video-with-person.mp4
OC_LOCAL_FACE_IMAGE=/path/to/person-reference.jpg
# Face-CLUSTER real-data e2e (test/e2e/live/cases/17_face_cluster.sh): a folder of
# curated CLEAN crops of TWO distinct people — willsmith_ref.jpg + willsmith_N.jpg
# (one person) and personB_N.jpg (another). The test ingests them, clusters, and
# checks a held-out identify picks the right person. If unset, that case falls back
# to ingesting OC_LOCAL_FACE_VIDEO (looser assertions). Needs the --face venv below.
OC_CLUSTER_FIXTURE_DIR=/path/to/face-crops
OC_LOCAL_IMAGE_REF=/path/to/logo-reference.jpg
OC_LOCAL_IMAGE_VIDEO_A=/path/to/candidate-a.mp4
OC_LOCAL_IMAGE_VIDEO_B=/path/to/candidate-b.mp4
# Local basic-clip (CLIP semantic) DB e2e (test/e2e/live/cases/17_clip_db.sh).
# ALL OPTIONAL — when unset, the case derives real fixtures itself: it clips
# OC_VIDEO_OBJECTS/OC_VIDEO_SMALL, extracts frames with ffmpeg, and captions a
# frame with `see` to produce the text queries.
# OC_CLIP_VIDEO=/path/to/scene-video.mp4          # video A override (embedded, frame-sampled)
# OC_CLIP_IMAGE_REF=/path/to/reference.jpg        # image-member override
# OC_CLIP_TEXT=a red car at night                 # fallback text query when `see` is unavailable
# Local audio-fp (Shazam fingerprint) + basic-clap (CLAP) DB e2e
# (test/e2e/live/cases/28_audio_match_local.sh + 29_clap_db.sh). Case 28 is
# self-contained (synthesizes its own chirp fixtures — no media needed). Case 29
# (CLAP) is HARD-GATED on OC_CLAP_E2E because the first run downloads ~776MB of
# model weights; leave it unset in CI.
# OC_CLAP_E2E=1                                    # opt in to the CLAP db e2e
# Local voice-print (speaker verification) DB e2e. Both cases are HARD-GATED on
# OC_VOICE_E2E (loads the pyannote/torch stack + downloads the ~26MB wespeaker
# model on first run).
#   34_voice_match.sh          — plumbing: synthetic macOS `say` voices (or set
#                                OC_VOICE_REF/OC_VOICE_CLIP to two different-speaker
#                                clips on Linux). TTS doesn't discriminate, so this
#                                only checks the verb wiring / modes / diarize tier.
#   35_voice_match_realmedia.sh — ACCURACY on real media: extract + enhance a
#                                snippet of the speaker, enroll their video, confirm
#                                it matches while a DIFFERENT video is rejected.
# OC_VOICE_E2E=1                                   # opt in to the voice match e2e
# OC_VOICE_REF=/path/to/speaker-a-sample.wav       # case 34 fixture overrides (Linux)
# OC_VOICE_CLIP=/path/to/speaker-b-clip.wav
# OC_VOICE_SPEAKER_VIDEO=/path/to/single-speaker.mp4  # case 35 source (else falls
#                                back to OC_LOCAL_FACE_VIDEO, then OC_VIDEO_SPEECH)
# OC_VOICE_OTHER_VIDEO=/path/to/different-speaker.mp4  # case 35 negative (else auto)
# Python for local image/face/CLIP/audio DB providers AND the local-models enhance
# toolbox (enhance --ops separate/segment). Recommended setup:
#   scripts/visual-db-uv.sh          # image DB deps
#   scripts/visual-db-uv.sh --face   # image + face DB deps
#   scripts/visual-db-uv.sh --clip   # CLIP (open_clip + torch) DB deps
#   scripts/visual-db-uv.sh --audio  # audio fingerprint (scipy) DB deps
#   scripts/visual-db-uv.sh --clap   # CLAP (transformers + torch) audio DB deps
#   scripts/visual-db-uv.sh --voice  # pyannote (enhance --ops separate + voice match)
#   scripts/visual-db-uv.sh --segment# transformers+SAM2/GroundingDINO (enhance --ops segment)
#   scripts/visual-db-uv.sh --enhance# both enhance stacks (--voice + --segment)
#   scripts/visual-db-uv.sh --all    # all of the above
# Then set this to the printed venv Python if you do not use the default path.
OC_VISUAL_DB_PY=
# Optional CLIP model overrides (defaults: ViT-B-32 / openai weights / cpu):
# OC_CLIP_MODEL=ViT-B-32
# OC_CLIP_PRETRAINED=openai
# OC_CLIP_DEVICE=cpu
# Optional CLAP model overrides (defaults: laion/larger_clap_general / cpu):
# OC_CLAP_MODEL=laion/larger_clap_general
# OC_CLAP_DEVICE=cpu
# Optional voice-print (speaker verification) overrides. The default embedding
# model is UNGATED (no HF_TOKEN needed); only `voice match --diarize` needs
# HF_TOKEN + the accepted pyannote pipeline license. The model is pinned per
# index at create time — changing it needs a new voice-print index.
# OVERCAST_VOICE_MODEL=pyannote/wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM
# OC_VOICE_DEVICE=cpu               # cpu|mps|cuda for voice embeddings (mps experimental)
# Optional enhance --ops separate/segment overrides (local-models + fal):
# OVERCAST_DIARIZE_MODEL=pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1
# SEGMENT_DETECT_MODEL=IDEA-Research/grounding-dino-tiny
# SEGMENT_SAM_MODEL=facebook/sam2.1-hiera-tiny
# SEGMENT_THRESHOLD=0.3           # GroundingDINO box threshold
# SEGMENT_MAX_INSTANCES=8         # cap masks PER CLASS (local + fal sam-3); a
#                                 # comma-prompt "person, car" yields up to N of each
# FAL_SEPARATE_MODEL=fal-ai/sam-audio/separate
# FAL_SEGMENT_MODEL=fal-ai/sam-3/image
# Optional LIVE e2e assertion thresholds. Normal CLI use can omit these and pass
# flags per command instead. Provider defaults when flags are omitted are:
# image min-inliers=15 min-ratio=0.4 max-frames=8; face min-similarity=68 max-frames=8.
# When fps is provided, max-frames becomes an optional cap.
# OC_LOCAL_IMAGE_MIN_INLIERS=8
# OC_LOCAL_IMAGE_MIN_RATIO=0.25
# OC_LOCAL_IMAGE_FPS=0.7
# OC_LOCAL_IMAGE_MAX_FRAMES=12
# OC_LOCAL_FACE_MIN_SIMILARITY=45
# OC_LOCAL_FACE_FPS=0.5
# OC_LOCAL_FACE_MAX_FRAMES=24

# ── Local object detector (see --detect) ──────────────────────────────────
# Python interpreter that has torch + transformers + scipy + pillow installed
# (OWLv2 / Grounding DINO). Build it with:
#   scripts/visual-db-uv.sh --detect     # (or --all for face + CLIP + detector)
# then set this to the printed venv Python. If unset, the case probes
# python3/python and skips when the deps aren't present. e.g. /path/to/venv/bin/python
DETECT_PY=
# Optional detector tuning (defaults shown):
# DETECT_MODEL=google/owlv2-base-patch16-ensemble
# DETECT_THRESHOLD=0.1
# DETECT_MAX_FRAMES=8

# ── Contact sheets (grid / grid --view) ─────────────────────────────────────
# grid tiles video frames into a contact sheet for one-shot VLM triage; it needs
# NO keys (pure ffmpeg — the see / frame-verify CoT steps reuse the brain +
# Cloudglue configured above). Burned cell labels need an ffmpeg built with
# drawtext (libfreetype); when a system font isn't auto-found, point this at a
# .ttf — else cells are numbered positionally (and `grid --view` labels them in
# CSS regardless). Leave unset unless you want labels burned into the PNG:
# OVERCAST_GRID_FONT=/System/Library/Fonts/Supplemental/Arial.ttf

# ── Runner knobs (env only; not secrets) ───────────────────────────────────
# OVERCAST_USE_NODE=1   # run `node dist/bin/overcast.js` instead of the bun binary
# SKIP_BUILD=1          # reuse an existing dist build (skip the build step)
# OC_TIMEOUT=300        # per-command timeout in seconds
# OC_E2E_CLAUDE=1       # opt in to 89_skill_claude: drive the real `claude` CLI
#                       # headless to run a skill (spends Claude credit + uses the
#                       # machine's Claude auth + runs Bash headless). Off by default.

# ── Man in the chair (/chair remote console) ────────────────────────────────
# Remote-drive the live TUI session from a phone (see docs/flows.md flow 23).
# ALL OPTIONAL and zero-config — `/chair on` works with the defaults below; no
# keys needed (it reuses the configured brain LLM + Node's built-in http). Reach
# it only over Tailscale/WireGuard or an SSH tunnel — there is no TLS.
# OVERCAST_CHAIR=1                # auto-start the bridge on TUI launch (same as --chair)
# OVERCAST_CHAIR_BIND=127.0.0.1   # bind address; keep off public ifaces (or use `/chair on tailnet`)
# OVERCAST_CHAIR_PORT=7373        # listen port
# OVERCAST_CHAIR_TOKEN=           # pin the pairing token (default: fresh random per `/chair on`)

# ── Report / wall opsec ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HTML briefs/status/records exports and the `wall` open in the analyst's
# browser. By default they NEVER load remote scraped media (a scan hit's thumb,
# an un-captured video URL): a CSP blocks it and the templates show a placeholder
# instead — otherwise opening a report would beacon your IP/timing to the
# investigated host. Set to 1 only when you accept that disclosure (e.g. on a
# throwaway/VPN box) to embed remote images/videos live.
# OVERCAST_REPORT_REMOTE_MEDIA=1
